    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-4-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 After subsection 471.27(1) of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-4-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nStrengthening child sex offences  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\n\n(1A) For the purposes of an offence against section 471.25A, absolute\nliability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the\noffence that the child is someone who is under 16.\nNote 1:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\nNote 2:\nFor a defence based on belief about age, see section 471.29.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\nStrengthening child sex offences  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\n\n(1A) For the purposes of an offence against section 471.25A, absolute\nliability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the\noffence that the child is someone who is under 16.\nNote 1:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\nNote 2:\nFor a defence based on belief about age, see section 471.29.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-4-sec-11-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-4-sec-11-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab8536141c23812fa5aa5003d58fc495243948108b1a6f31042ff8ba160582af",
      "skos:note": "Absolute liability applies for an offence against section 471.25A when the child is under 16."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-4-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 After subsection 471.27(1) of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nStrengthening child sex offences  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\n\n(1A) For the purposes of an offence against section 471.25A, absolute\nliability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the\noffence that the child is someone who is under 16.\nNote 1:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\nNote 2:\nFor a defence based on belief about age, see section 471.29."
    },
    {
