    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(4) After section 15AA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-7-sec-4-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the Director of Public\nProsecutions or the person may appeal against a decision of a bail\nauthority:\n\n(a) to grant bail to the person despite subsection (1) on the basis\nthat the bail authority is satisfied that circumstances exist to\ngrant bail; or\n\n(b) to refuse to grant bail to the person on the basis that the bail\nauthority is not satisfied that circumstances exist to grant\nbail.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the Director of Public\nProsecutions or the person may appeal against a decision of a bail\nauthority:\n\n(a) to grant bail to the person despite subsection (1) on the basis\nthat the bail authority is satisfied that circumstances exist to\ngrant bail; or\n\n(b) to refuse to grant bail to the person on the basis that the bail\nauthority is not satisfied that circumstances exist to grant\nbail.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a244b2bfbd2c64f1bef6fedde9aa55f511467f7f11e6accaaca3f204112e2bec",
      "skos:note": "Appeal against a decision of a bail authority to grant or refuse bail."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-7-sec-4-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(4) After section 15AA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the Director of Public\nProsecutions or the person may appeal against a decision of a bail\nauthority:\n\n(a) to grant bail to the person despite subsection (1) on the basis\nthat the bail authority is satisfied that circumstances exist to\ngrant bail; or\n\n(b) to refuse to grant bail to the person on the basis that the bail\nauthority is not satisfied that circumstances exist to grant\nbail."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
