    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 After subsection 16A(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-8-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2AAA) In determining the sentence to be passed, or the order to be made,\nin respect of any person for a Commonwealth child sex offence, in\naddition to any other matters, the court must have regard to the\nobjective of rehabilitating the person, including by considering\nwhether it is appropriate, taking into account such of the following\nmatters as are relevant and known to the court:\n\n(a) when making an order—to impose any conditions about\nrehabilitation or treatment options;\n\n(b) in determining the length of any sentence or non-parole\nperiod—to include sufficient time for the person to undertake\na rehabilitation program.\n\nSchedule 8  Matters court has regard to when passing sentence etc.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(2AAA) In determining the sentence to be passed, or the order to be made,\nin respect of any person for a Commonwealth child sex offence, in\naddition to any other matters, the court must have regard to the\nobjective of rehabilitating the person, including by considering\nwhether it is appropriate, taking into account such of the following\nmatters as are relevant and known to the court:\n\n(a) when making an order—to impose any conditions about\nrehabilitation or treatment options;\n\n(b) in determining the length of any sentence or non-parole\nperiod—to include sufficient time for the person to undertake\na rehabilitation program.\n\nSchedule 8  Matters court has regard to when passing sentence etc.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-logic-argumentation-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9cde076fbb043f6dbdf01ef75536cae3ef0e1bcf8c49f391efa09ec8cab9eef7",
      "skos:note": "Court must consider rehabilitation when passing sentence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-8-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 After subsection 16A(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2AAA) In determining the sentence to be passed, or the order to be made,\nin respect of any person for a Commonwealth child sex offence, in\naddition to any other matters, the court must have regard to the\nobjective of rehabilitating the person, including by considering\nwhether it is appropriate, taking into account such of the following\nmatters as are relevant and known to the court:\n\n(a) when making an order—to impose any conditions about\nrehabilitation or treatment options;\n\n(b) in determining the length of any sentence or non-parole\nperiod—to include sufficient time for the person to undertake\na rehabilitation program.\n\nSchedule 8  Matters court has regard to when passing sentence etc.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-8-sec-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
