      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "includes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Includes temporal intervals for revocation time",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the time at which the court determines the new offence was most likely to have been committed;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-3-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is an ordered trace of",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines order for revocation time intervals",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the time at which the court determines the new offence was most likely to have first begun to have been committed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must be one of",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must choose from three options for revocation time",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "one of the following times:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AQ(4) Parole order or licence revoked following further offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the parole order or licence relating to a person is taken to have\nbeen revoked under subsection (1) or (2), the person becomes\nliable to serve:\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020\n\n(a) that part of the sentence or of each sentence for a federal\noffence that the person had not served at the time of his or\nher release under that order or licence; or\n\n(b) if the court considers it appropriate taking into account the\ngood behaviour of the person during the period (the clean\nstreet period) starting at the time the person was released\nunder that order or licence and ending at the revocation\ntime—the sentence or aggregate sentence that would be\nimposed under paragraph (a) reduced by the period that is the\nsame as the clean street period.\nSuspended sentences",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If the parole order or licence relating to a person is taken to have\nbeen revoked under subsection (1) or (2), the person becomes\nliable to serve:\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020\n\n(a) that part of the sentence or of each sentence for a federal\noffence that the person had not served at the time of his or\nher release under that order or licence; or\n\n(b) if the court considers it appropriate taking into account the\ngood behaviour of the person during the period (the clean\nstreet period) starting at the time the person was released\nunder that order or licence and ending at the revocation\ntime—the sentence or aggregate sentence that would be\nimposed under paragraph (a) reduced by the period that is the\nsame as the clean street period.\nSuspended sentences",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a4c29cea6bf72027bd0cd7ee1989350cd730bb2da91b3d499b99dd868b8c4cc",
      "skos:note": "Parole order or licence revoked following further offence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AQ(4) Parole order or licence revoked following further offence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the parole order or licence relating to a person is taken to have\nbeen revoked under subsection (1) or (2), the person becomes\nliable to serve:\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020\n\n(a) that part of the sentence or of each sentence for a federal\noffence that the person had not served at the time of his or\nher release under that order or licence; or\n\n(b) if the court considers it appropriate taking into account the\ngood behaviour of the person during the period (the clean\nstreet period) starting at the time the person was released\nunder that order or licence and ending at the revocation\ntime—the sentence or aggregate sentence that would be\nimposed under paragraph (a) reduced by the period that is the\nsame as the clean street period.\nSuspended sentences"
    },
