    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Subsections 19AR(1) and (2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nNew federal offence etc.\n\n(1) Subject to subsection (4), if:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence or\nfederal offences committed during the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\nRevocation of parole order or licence  Schedule 13\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthe court imposing the new sentence or sentences:\n\n(d) must not make a recognizance release order; and\n\n(e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the new\nsentence or sentences and the outstanding sentence or\nsentences having regard to the total period of imprisonment\nthat the person is liable to serve.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nNew federal offence etc.\n\n(1) Subject to subsection (4), if:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence or\nfederal offences committed during the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\nRevocation of parole order or licence  Schedule 13\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthe court imposing the new sentence or sentences:\n\n(d) must not make a recognizance release order; and\n\n(e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the new\nsentence or sentences and the outstanding sentence or\nsentences having regard to the total period of imprisonment\nthat the person is liable to serve.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8a902efeba4290f256b95ce2cd9b467aa2b26cc23397877abf74c3580458d70a",
      "skos:note": "Court must not make a recognizance release order for certain individuals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Subsections 19AR(1) and (2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nNew federal offence etc.\n\n(1) Subject to subsection (4), if:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence or\nfederal offences committed during the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\nRevocation of parole order or licence  Schedule 13\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthe court imposing the new sentence or sentences:\n\n(d) must not make a recognizance release order; and\n\n(e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the new\nsentence or sentences and the outstanding sentence or\nsentences having regard to the total period of imprisonment\nthat the person is liable to serve."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
