      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court must not make a recognizance release order.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Subsection 19AR(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nNew State or Territory offence etc.\n\n(3) Subject to subsection (4), if:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more State or\nTerritory offences committed during the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthe court imposing the new sentence or sentences:\n\n(d) must not make a recognizance release order; and\n\n(e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the\noutstanding sentence or sentences having regard to the total\nperiod of imprisonment that the person is liable to serve.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nNew State or Territory offence etc.\n\n(3) Subject to subsection (4), if:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more State or\nTerritory offences committed during the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthe court imposing the new sentence or sentences:\n\n(d) must not make a recognizance release order; and\n\n(e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the\noutstanding sentence or sentences having regard to the total\nperiod of imprisonment that the person is liable to serve.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f8e9d307bd8b9b5c75b6dd9805f57457d9ed7ae0ba8e2465f2f06f23555d953f",
      "skos:note": "Court must not make a recognizance release order for certain individuals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Subsection 19AR(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nNew State or Territory offence etc.\n\n(3) Subject to subsection (4), if:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more State or\nTerritory offences committed during the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthe court imposing the new sentence or sentences:\n\n(d) must not make a recognizance release order; and\n\n(e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the\noutstanding sentence or sentences having regard to the total\nperiod of imprisonment that the person is liable to serve."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-8"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-8-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must Not",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court must not make a recognizance release order.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Court imposes new sentence or sentences.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Recognizance release order is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Subsection 19AR(4)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral\n\n(4) A court may decline to fix a non-parole period if:\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that doing so is appropriate, having\nregard to:\n\n(i) the serious nature and circumstances of the offence or\noffences; and\n\n(ii) the antecedents of the person; or\n\n(b) the person is expected to be serving a State or Territory\nsentence on the day after the end of the federal sentence, or\nthe last to be served of the federal sentences, as reduced by\nany remissions or reductions under section 19AA.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral\n\n(4) A court may decline to fix a non-parole period if:\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that doing so is appropriate, having\nregard to:\n\n(i) the serious nature and circumstances of the offence or\noffences; and\n\n(ii) the antecedents of the person; or\n\n(b) the person is expected to be serving a State or Territory\nsentence on the day after the end of the federal sentence, or\nthe last to be served of the federal sentences, as reduced by\nany remissions or reductions under section 19AA.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-9-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "40b65da92507f7fed6b4f18b3c051c9c6a8e1eae5a39e4fbbe07b1b39929338b",
      "skos:note": "A court may decline to fix a non-parole period if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Subsection 19AR(4)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral\n\n(4) A court may decline to fix a non-parole period if:\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that doing so is appropriate, having\nregard to:\n\n(i) the serious nature and circumstances of the offence or\noffences; and\n\n(ii) the antecedents of the person; or\n\n(b) the person is expected to be serving a State or Territory\nsentence on the day after the end of the federal sentence, or\nthe last to be served of the federal sentences, as reduced by\nany remissions or reductions under section 19AA."
    },
