      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal,\nState or Territory offences committed during the parole\nperiod or licence period; and\n\n(ba) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal,\nState or Territory offences committed during the parole\nperiod or licence period; and\n\n(ba) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-17-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-17-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "25d109730186582f39e6d12e82695aaf5a3a929aa8685991ec0f18906af15600",
      "skos:note": "A person serving a federal sentence must be released on parole or licence under this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Paragraphs 19AT(1)(a) and (b)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal,\nState or Territory offences committed during the parole\nperiod or licence period; and\n\n(ba) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\n\nSchedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020"
    },
