    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Application provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by items 1, 4, 5 and 7 to 17 of this Schedule\napply in relation to the revocation, on or after the commencement of\nthis Schedule, of a parole order or licence relating to a sentence that was\nimposed on a person (whether the sentence was imposed before, on or\nafter that commencement).\n(2)\nThe amendment made by item 2 of this Schedule applies in relation to\nfixing, on or after the commencement of this Schedule, a non-parole\nperiod in respect of a sentence (whether the sentence was imposed\nbefore, on or after that commencement).\n(3)\nThe amendments made by items 18 and 19 of this Schedule apply in\nrelation to hearings begun on or after the commencement of this\nSchedule (whether the order revoking the relevant parole order or\nlicence was made before, on or after that commencement).\n\nDefinitions  Schedule 14\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments made by items 1, 4, 5 and 7 to 17 of this Schedule\napply in relation to the revocation, on or after the commencement of\nthis Schedule, of a parole order or licence relating to a sentence that was\nimposed on a person (whether the sentence was imposed before, on or\nafter that commencement).\n(2)\nThe amendment made by item 2 of this Schedule applies in relation to\nfixing, on or after the commencement of this Schedule, a non-parole\nperiod in respect of a sentence (whether the sentence was imposed\nbefore, on or after that commencement).\n(3)\nThe amendments made by items 18 and 19 of this Schedule apply in\nrelation to hearings begun on or after the commencement of this\nSchedule (whether the order revoking the relevant parole order or\nlicence was made before, on or after that commencement).\n\nDefinitions  Schedule 14\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b973a177e8d2f8696a53d64680f121ab0d45fbb276af8f0a49ee4f523c6c542",
      "skos:note": "Amendments apply in relation to revocation of parole orders or licences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-13-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Application provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by items 1, 4, 5 and 7 to 17 of this Schedule\napply in relation to the revocation, on or after the commencement of\nthis Schedule, of a parole order or licence relating to a sentence that was\nimposed on a person (whether the sentence was imposed before, on or\nafter that commencement).\n(2)\nThe amendment made by item 2 of this Schedule applies in relation to\nfixing, on or after the commencement of this Schedule, a non-parole\nperiod in respect of a sentence (whether the sentence was imposed\nbefore, on or after that commencement).\n(3)\nThe amendments made by items 18 and 19 of this Schedule apply in\nrelation to hearings begun on or after the commencement of this\nSchedule (whether the order revoking the relevant parole order or\nlicence was made before, on or after that commencement).\n\nDefinitions  Schedule 14\n\nNo. 70, 2020\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020"
    },
