    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-14-sec-272",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "272 18, 272.19, 273.7, 471.22, 474.23A or 474.24A,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-14-sec-272"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "subsection 474.25A(1) or (2) or section 474.25B or 474.25C of the\nCriminal Code.\nState or Territory registrable child sex offence means an offence:\n\n(a) that a person becomes, or may at any time have become, a\nperson whose name is entered on a child protection offender\nregister (however described) of a State or Territory for\ncommitting; and\n\n(b) in respect of which:\n\n(i) a child was a victim or an intended victim; or\n\n(ii) the offending involved child abuse material.\n\nSchedule 15  Review of sentencing for Commonwealth child sex offences\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020",
      "skos:definition": "subsection 474.25A(1) or (2) or section 474.25B or 474.25C of the\nCriminal Code.\nState or Territory registrable child sex offence means an offence:\n\n(a) that a person becomes, or may at any time have become, a\nperson whose name is entered on a child protection offender\nregister (however described) of a State or Territory for\ncommitting; and\n\n(b) in respect of which:\n\n(i) a child was a victim or an intended victim; or\n\n(ii) the offending involved child abuse material.\n\nSchedule 15  Review of sentencing for Commonwealth child sex offences\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-14-sec-272-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-14-sec-272-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c2c0c60f26c032a6d1e96f68f083748ccb77c78b462ebff277b32b29f83ec01",
      "skos:note": "State or Territory registrable child sex offence means an offence that a person becomes, or may at any time have become, a person whose name is entered on a child protection offender register."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-14-sec-272",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "272 18, 272.19, 273.7, 471.22, 474.23A or 474.24A,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "subsection 474.25A(1) or (2) or section 474.25B or 474.25C of the\nCriminal Code.\nState or Territory registrable child sex offence means an offence:\n\n(a) that a person becomes, or may at any time have become, a\nperson whose name is entered on a child protection offender\nregister (however described) of a State or Territory for\ncommitting; and\n\n(b) in respect of which:\n\n(i) a child was a victim or an intended victim; or\n\n(ii) the offending involved child abuse material.\n\nSchedule 15  Review of sentencing for Commonwealth child sex offences\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and\nCommunity Protection Measures) Act 2020\nNo. 70, 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-14-sec-272-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-14-sec-272"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-14-sec-272-logic-descriptionlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the offence based on its relation to a child protection offender register.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The offence is committed by a person whose name is entered on a child protection offender register.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Therefore, the offence is registrable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-15-sec-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 Review of sentencing for Commonwealth child sex",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-15-sec-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2020a00070.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2020a00070.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "offences\n(1)\nThe Attorney-General must cause a review to be undertaken of the first\n3 years of the operation of the following provisions of Part IB\n(sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders) of the\nCrimes Act 1914, as amended by this Act, in relation to Commonwealth\nchild sex offences (within the meaning of that Act):\n\n(a) Divisions 2 to 4;\n\n(b) Subdivision D of Division 5;\n\n(c) Divisions 6 to 9;\n\n(d) Division 1, to the extent that it relates to a provision covered\nby paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of this subitem.\n(2)\nThe review must be undertaken by one or more persons who, in the\nAttorney-General’s opinion, possess appropriate qualifications to\nundertake the review.\n(3)\nThe person or persons undertaking the review must give the\nAttorney-General a written report of the review within 12 months after\nthe end of the 3-year period.\n(4)\nThe Attorney-General must cause a copy of the report of the review to\nbe laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of\nthat House after its receipt by the Attorney-General.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 11 September 2019\nSenate on 17 October 2019]\n\n(169/19)",
      "skos:definition": "offences\n(1)\nThe Attorney-General must cause a review to be undertaken of the first\n3 years of the operation of the following provisions of Part IB\n(sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders) of the\nCrimes Act 1914, as amended by this Act, in relation to Commonwealth\nchild sex offences (within the meaning of that Act):\n\n(a) Divisions 2 to 4;\n\n(b) Subdivision D of Division 5;\n\n(c) Divisions 6 to 9;\n\n(d) Division 1, to the extent that it relates to a provision covered\nby paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of this subitem.\n(2)\nThe review must be undertaken by one or more persons who, in the\nAttorney-General’s opinion, possess appropriate qualifications to\nundertake the review.\n(3)\nThe person or persons undertaking the review must give the\nAttorney-General a written report of the review within 12 months after\nthe end of the 3-year period.\n(4)\nThe Attorney-General must cause a copy of the report of the review to\nbe laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of\nthat House after its receipt by the Attorney-General.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 11 September 2019\nSenate on 17 October 2019]\n\n(169/19)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-15-sec-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-15-sec-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-15-sec-1-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-15-sec-1-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2020a00070-sch-15-sec-1-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "115b815f4252e76a6a926313c7ce0b66876ee2a9a416e070148bdc0954013a5f",
      "skos:note": "Review of sentencing for Commonwealth child sex offences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2020a00070#sch-15-sec-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 Review of sentencing for Commonwealth child sex",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "offences\n(1)\nThe Attorney-General must cause a review to be undertaken of the first\n3 years of the operation of the following provisions of Part IB\n(sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders) of the\nCrimes Act 1914, as amended by this Act, in relation to Commonwealth\nchild sex offences (within the meaning of that Act):\n\n(a) Divisions 2 to 4;\n\n(b) Subdivision D of Division 5;\n\n(c) Divisions 6 to 9;\n\n(d) Division 1, to the extent that it relates to a provision covered\nby paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of this subitem.\n(2)\nThe review must be undertaken by one or more persons who, in the\nAttorney-General’s opinion, possess appropriate qualifications to\nundertake the review.\n(3)\nThe person or persons undertaking the review must give the\nAttorney-General a written report of the review within 12 months after\nthe end of the 3-year period.\n(4)\nThe Attorney-General must cause a copy of the report of the review to\nbe laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of\nthat House after its receipt by the Attorney-General.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 11 September 2019\nSenate on 17 October 2019]\n\n(169/19)"
    },
